        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Sealing a deck typically costs roughly $0.30 to $0.80 per square foot in materials if you do it yourself and roughly $1.50 to $3.50 per square foot if you hire a pro for a standard clean and seal. For a 300-square-foot deck, that is about $100 to $250 DIY and about $450 to $1,050 hired, with stripping, sanding and lots of railing pushing costs higher. Prices vary by region and change over time, so use these as planning ranges.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The cheapest deck over the long run is the one you keep up with. Choose a sealer by cost per year of protection, not price per gallon, reseal when the water test says the finish is wearing, and you will rarely face the expensive stripping job that turns a few hundred dollars of maintenance into a much bigger bill.
          </p>
